  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "LJpegDecompressor::decode",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/decompressors/LJpegDecompressor.cpp",
    "description": "`decode()` validates `offsetX/offsetY` by casting attacker-controlled `uint32` values to `int` before bounds checks (`if (static_cast<int>(offsetX) >= mRaw->dim.x)`). Large unsigned offsets (e.g. >= 2^31) become negative as `int`, bypass the checks, and are stored in `offX/offY`. Later in `decodeN<4>()`, `offY + y` is used to compute the destination row pointer via `mRaw->getDataUncropped(offX, destY)` and then written through (`*dest++ = ...`), causing wild out-of-bounds writes and ASan SEGV at line 135.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer input controls raw-image metadata and the three u32 values read before JPEG data; supplying a huge `offsetX`/`offsetY` that overflows signed conversion in `LJpegDecompressor::decode()` is sufficient. The JPEG stream must parse far enough to reach `decodeScan()`/`decodeN<4>()` (as in PoC with SOI/SOF3/DHT/SOS and 4 components). Then decode writes to a pointer derived from unchecked wrapped offsets, triggering the crash."
  },
